{"name":"Gulf Breeze","hex":"#ddded3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gulf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hollow place in the earth; an abyss; a deep chasm or basin.","That which swallows; the gullet."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To engulf.","To award a degree to somebody who has only just passed sufficiently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gulf"},{"term":"breeze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A light, gentle wind.","Any activity that is easy, not testing or difficult."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move casually, in a carefree manner.","To blow gently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breeze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gulf Breeze (train)","blocks":[{"text":"The Gulf Breeze was a daily passenger train operated by Amtrak between New York City and Mobile, Alabama, as a section of the Crescent. Southbound, the Gulf Breeze split from the Crescent in Birmingham to serve an additional seven stations in Alabama on a 275-mile (443 km) route south to Mobile. The service ran from 1989 until 1995."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Amtrak_Gulf_Breeze_at_Montgomery_station%2C_June_1990.jpg/330px-Amtrak_Gulf_Breeze_at_Montgomery_station%2C_June_1990.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gulf_Breeze_(train)"},{"title":"Gulf Breeze, Florida","blocks":[{"text":"Gulf Breeze is a city in Santa Rosa County, Florida. It is located between Downtown Pensacola and Pensacola Beach, and is part of the Pensacola Metropolitan Area. The population was 6,340 at the 2020 census, up from 5,763 at the 2010 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/View_from_ISS_Expedition_72%2C_Gulf_Breeze%2C_Florida%2C_November_19%2C_2024_%28ISS072-E-98035%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-View_from_ISS_Expedition_72%2C_Gulf_Breeze%2C_Florida%2C_November_19%2C_2024_%28ISS072-E-98035%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gulf_Breeze%2C_Florida"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Gulf_Breeze_at_Montgomery%2C_March_26%2C_1995.jpg/330px-Gulf_Breeze_at_Montgomery%2C_March_26%2C_1995.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Gulf_Breeze_at_Montgomery%2C_March_26%2C_1995.jpg/330px-Gulf_Breeze_at_Montgomery%2C_March_26%2C_1995.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Gulf Breeze at Montgomery in March 1995, days before being discontinued","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGulf_Breeze_at_Montgomery%2C_March_26%2C_1995.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/GulfBreezeHS.JPG/500px-GulfBreezeHS.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/GulfBreezeHS.JPG/1280px-GulfBreezeHS.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa